From 599c54b9c57e7d1842eb0d7baabd4e9143fccdcc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 14:32:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Add failing tests for HTTP-1 and HTTP-8 worker starvation

Acceptance scenarios (tests/integration/test_http_worker_fairness_flow.cpp):
keep-alive holding, trickled bodies, idle connects, unauthenticated large
upload, per-connection request and lifetime caps, per-client worker share
with the trusted-proxy exemption, and prompt shutdown with parked
connections. Unit scenarios for the new net::ConnectionParker, the
server.http.request_threads key, and the outbound caps following the
configured pool.

The API surface (HttpServeTuning, HttpConnectionDispatcher, the parker) is
declared with red-phase stubs so the suite compiles and fails on the
current behaviour; the implementation follows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016DoEHHqJeaGBekj7YUaatB
