From 8c10a5f66881cbd616ca7f8603267dd32ff0324c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 14:46:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Serve HTTP through a connection dispatcher; configurable
 request pool (HTTP-1, HTTP-8)

- No worker waits on a quiet connection: new and kept-alive connections are
  parked on one poll thread (net::ConnectionParker) and dispatched only when
  readable (or with pipelined / TLS-buffered input), at most one per worker
  and at most max(1, pool/4) per client address; trusted proxies are exempt
  from the per-client share. First-byte and idle timeouts are enforced by the
  dispatcher.
- Minimum body rate: after a 10 s grace the body must have delivered
  16 KiB/s x (elapsed - grace), else 408; replaces the 30 s + len/16 KiB
  deadline and the 5 s body inter-byte gap.
- A media upload over the general body cap is read under max_upload_size only
  when its head authenticates; otherwise 401 M_MISSING_TOKEN/M_UNKNOWN_TOKEN
  before any of the body is read, then close.
- HTTP-8: Connection: close after 1000 requests or 1 hour per connection.
- server.http.request_threads (4..256, default 16, restart required) sizes
  the main pool; the ADR-0079 outbound caps follow it.
- TLS: the handshake runs on a worker once the ClientHello is readable; TLS
  input OpenSSL already buffered is no longer missed by poll().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016DoEHHqJeaGBekj7YUaatB
